y need to figure out what's going on  before that happens and it disappears  forever and when they examine the  countdown they realize they have about  four hours until it happens at one point  they encounter an energy barrier and  salvo is able to disable that because  she worked on the fence which is a newer  form of the same kind of technology and  figuring that out means that now they  need her because they're probably gonna  run into more of these and so when they  try to overtake the enacrions when they  try to rebel and get their weapons which  doesn't work out she gets to live and  with that story that's pretty much where  things are left  on the emperor's ship outside of the  salt palace we see that brother day's in  a pretty bad mood after her lima speech  demerizel explains to him that if she  hadn't knelt it would have been a clear  contradiction of her faith and they have  an argument about where her loyalties  lie he points out here that her being a  robot is a secret he says i wonder what  halima would say if she were made aware  that demarzel can't be reincarnated  either and he says that her actions were  a betrayal a betrayal of her directive  as far as he understood it she was  incapable of disloyalty her fealty to  the clionic dynasty should be above all  else that should be embedded into her  programming and she does counter all of  his points explaining that if kneeling  were against her protocols she wouldn't  have been able to do it at all there  just wouldn't have been a way that she  could have physically so there's tension  there i believe as viewers we're  supposed to wonder about her actual  loyalty just in the same way he is but  they're interrupted as one of his aides  comes in to tell him that halima's  speech had struck a chord and she's now  the front-runner to become the next  proxima when they go to talk to her we  get a glimpse of some pilgrims who tried  to walk the spiral or maybe some of them  actually completed it but you see that  they get pretty beat up in the process  we find out that demarzel actually did  it she did it many years ago and that  many people die trying to do it he tries  to bargain with halima he wants to know  what her ask is what she needs to back  off of calling him soulless and  undermining his authority and her answer  is that she wants him to end the genetic  dynasty she says it's not a tactic and  that she really does believe that the  dynasty has to end back on the ship  brother day acknowledges that harry  selden predicted a split with one of the  major religions essentially that  luminism would go against the genetic  dynasty demarzel tries to assert her  loyalty she's ready to play defense and  protect the empire from halimah's  message but dae has a different plan he  plans to prove halima and harry seldom  wrong he goes back to see her and he  declares that he'll appeal to the triple  goddesses themselves he'll walk the  spiral and he'll let them decide what is  true who is right and who is wrong and  that's where his story ends for the  episode and he set up to do that next  time  back at the palace on trantor brother  dawn and azora are escalating their  relationship we see her leave a message  that leads to him finding her for a  rendezvous where they have sex for the  first time she tries to give him a  device that would correct his color  blindness and then he explains why he  would never be able to use that if the  other cleons found out if they noticed  what he was doing then they might notice  all the other ways he's different which  he fires off and there are quite a few  of them to show her just how important  it is that they don't find out he takes  her back to the palace where he shows  her the original klee on the first and  then takes her into this back room we  hadn't seen before  where they keep replacement backups for  all of them just in case something  happens  his reason for existing the reason that  they cloned them in the first place is  for them to be perfect copies of the  original if they can't do that then they  have to be destroyed and their last day  would be their replacements first day  she tries to suggest that he should run  away and she has an answer to every  reason he throws out there that he  thinks it wouldn't work she tries to  tell him about where she lives it's  called the scar the area where the star  bridge fell where the lower levels were  opened up and they can actually see  outside she points out how different it  is in the palace and how everything's  alive and it's waiting for him and she  really tries to sell him on it saying  that they can change his face and they  can drain his nano bots and we'll have  to see how that plays out because i  don't know if any of that will turn out  to be possible or not a little later  whenever he misses the dinner bell  brother dusk comes looking for him where  he makes the excuse that he was trying  to learn about trantor and dusk just  says we are trantor nothing outside the  palace walls is relevant and their story  ends there  and in the final storyline we finally  get back to gail and what's going on  with harry on the raven the harry selden  quantum consciousness protocol which  eventually stops glitching she's able to  talk to him and he comes back and we  find out that he had a data unit  implanted in his brain before they left  trantor and he finds out that they're on  the raven heading to helicon rach was  supposed to be there gail was supposed  to be on terminus to lead the first  foundation and when he finds out that  lewis is in charge he says that that  would be fine to get them through the  settlement stage but they'll need  someone else for what comes next they'll  be facing the first crisis soon which  we've seen that they are in fact facing  she explains why she's there what  happened that rach has been executed and  for a while he starts glitching out  again and when he leaves this time the  life support systems bli