t she needs to to stop a  micro meteor right as it breaches the  ship's hall they realized that harry  couldn't predict that she was going to  be there because whatever gives her this  ability is beyond normal human behavior  she's different and she describes it  saying that she thinks she can feel the  future as the episode comes to an end  overall i think this is one of the  better episodes as i said at the  beginning i do think that it did a much  better job of bouncing back and forth  between the storylines and by including  them all it felt like more happened i  think one place where this show has  really struggled it's keeping up its  momentum they throw out these different  mysteries and different ideas and they  let them dangle for too long so this  seemed a lot more promising the  interiors of the ship look great i mean  they look fantastic i think the expanse  kind of ruined me for scenes with no  gravity because they do those so well  but everything looked okay in that  department here and i did think that the  sequence where pharah shot dorwan was  excellent that actually looked pretty  convincing harry coming back seems okay  in the big picture it's a pretty big  change but it felt like it would be  weird to have him come back like he did  in the books because they would have  been under utilizing jared harris if you  have him you should probably use him  because you see how he elevates scenes  because he's harry selden you can't help  but wonder what's going on with him so i  found myself really engaged with all the  scenes with him and gail and the setup  seems to work for where i think they're  going with it as far as her abilities  and the whole thing about her feeling  the future i hope they don't drag that  out i hope that she gets some  understanding i also really liked how  the focus is starting to shift from the  emperors to demarzo the actor that plays  halima did a great job with that role  her exchanges with lee pacer great he  does a great 